Description: Report xdg_toplevel.set_minimized on the IPC event stream
 niri has no minimized state and ignores a client's minimize request, so
 the minimize button of Firefox, GTK, Qt and every other third-party app
 does nothing. This adds one event-stream event, WindowMinimizeRequested
 { id }, sent when a mapped toplevel asks to be minimized. niri itself
 still leaves the window where it is: the Lulo OS Dock hears the event and
 minimizes the window the way the yellow traffic light of an rmac app
 does (record where it was, take its thumbnail while it is on screen, move
 it to the hidden "rmac-parking" workspace). The event is transient (not
 in the replicated state), and clients that match on event names, as rmac
 does, ignore it when they do not know it.
 .
 See docs/decisions/0021-niri-minimize-request.md in the rmac repository.
Author: Jacob Samas <samasjacob@icloud.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-25
